  "conclusions": [
    "Physical-row SFA permutation is calculated once per selected producer route and stored 32 bytes after its physical-row slot; all 14 CPU16 Q0 store copies load that cache and combine the SF-only field.",
    "The seven producer copies are compiler unroll sites, not seven runtime routes. Each admitted selected route still has one cached-base store.",
    "CPU16 adds a shared-address add and broadcast shared load for each consumed route/SF iteration. H4096 means eight iterations per lane; do not reinterpret 32 lanes as 32 memory transactions.",
    "Unsigned prefix calculation emitted add 127 then shr.u32 by 7, followed by accumulation. General signed quotient/remainder correction disappeared from the entire prefix.",
    "Prefix unrolling changed from an eight-site loop to 72 straightline loads; varied Q0 unroll copies increased from 3 to 7. These are observable code-shape changes; no exact cubin-byte attribution is established.",
    "REG 168, STACK 112 and SHARED 1024 are unchanged; PTX/cubin grew by 25,213/11,368 bytes. Neither resource stability nor smaller hot arithmetic establishes speed, occupancy improvement or GPU correctness."
  ]
